::CW_U03_L08_GP_Q01::Passage: The narrator dismisses an old map until it reveals the route her grandmother walked when first arriving in the city. What Unit 3 skill is most directly tested?{
~A. Random punctuation memorization.#Incorrect. The question focuses on fiction meaning, not punctuation.
~B. A recipe comparison.#Incorrect. No recipe appears.
=C. Coming-of-age changed understanding supported by a meaningful object.#Correct. The narrator's view changes because the map reveals family history.
~D. A theme with no evidence.#Incorrect. The map is evidence.
}
::CW_U03_L08_GP_Q02::Source element: A guide gives a traveler an object before a difficult journey. Adaptation: A coach gives a runner a marked-up route card before a city race. What is transformed?{
=A. The guide-object pattern becomes a modern coaching moment.#Correct. The source role remains, but setting and object change.
~B. The source is copied word for word.#Incorrect. It is transformed.
~C. The guide disappears completely.#Incorrect. The coach acts as guide.
~D. The journey becomes unrelated.#Incorrect. The race is the journey.
}
::CW_U03_L08_GP_Q03::Central idea: Secrets can damage trust. Which detail best supports it?{
~A. The room has a ceiling.#Incorrect. This does not support the idea.
~B. The character likes lunch.#Incorrect. This is unrelated.
~C. The sidewalk is gray.#Incorrect. Color alone does not support the idea.
=D. The character deletes a message before a friend sees it.#Correct. The hidden message shows secrecy between friends.
}
::CW_U03_L08_GP_Q04::Passage: "Naturally, the council chose the plan that fixed nothing and congratulated itself for efficiency." What rhetoric is most evident?{
~A. Neutral praise.#Incorrect. The tone is not neutral or praising.
=B. Sarcastic tone criticizing the council.#Correct. The wording says one thing while clearly criticizing.
~C. A direct recipe.#Incorrect. No recipe appears.
~D. A source adaptation only.#Incorrect. The focus is rhetoric.
}
::CW_U03_L08_GP_Q05::Passage: Mara thinks leaving home means losing everything. When she packs her grandmother's recipe card first, she realizes memory can travel with her. What theme is best supported?{
~A. Recipes erase memory.#Incorrect. The recipe preserves memory.
~B. Moving means forgetting everyone.#Incorrect. Mara carries memory with her.
=C. Change can include carrying meaningful parts of the past forward.#Correct. The recipe card helps Mara reframe leaving.
~D. Home has no meaning.#Incorrect. Home remains emotionally important.
}
